## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates expertise in architecting secure, scalable data science environments with strict least-privilege controls across multi-account data lakes, requiring mastery of ABAC, Lake Formation, KMS, and private networking.

## Key Concepts
- Attribute-based access control (ABAC) with IAM policy tags
- Lake Formation fine-grained permissions
- SageMaker notebook cross-account trust relationships
- Private connectivity through VPC endpoints
- Centralized CMK with rotation policies
- Immutable audit logging via CloudTrail
- Automated drift and privilege-creep detection

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/project}/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/dataset": "${aws:PrincipalTag/dataset}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical, implementable security controls for multi-tenant data on AWS, focusing on least-privilege access, data at rest encryption, and rapid breach containment.

## Key Concepts

- STS AssumeRole with tenant-scoped attributes
- S3 bucket policy and per-tenant prefixes for isolation
- KMS per-tenant CMKs with rotation
- CloudTrail data events for auditability
- 60-second containment workflow to revoke credentials and quarantine tenant data

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket/tenant-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:prefix": "tenant/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

